{"slug":"real-racing-3","title":"Real Racing 3","desc":"iOS / Android, Firemonkeys / EA 2013","notes":["Made from OBJ exports of the game's car models (3ds Max OBJ, one folder per car: <name>.obj = the car, <name> int.obj = the in-car model) and the game's textures of each car as PNG (ETC / PVRTC pictures decoded) with its liveries.  112 cars; folder names are the game's car names.","TEXTURES ARE NOT EMBEDDED: every car folder has a 'textures' folder (the FBX points there with relative paths): the game's pictures of the car and ALL its liveries (<car>_ext_<name>.etc.png).  The FBX and the render use one livery: a red one when the car has one, else the plain one, else the first.  Glass, tyres, brake discs and the chassis have no picture in the export: plain colours here.","Inside the FBX: Body + Wheels = LOD_A, the model the game shows close up (visible).  HIDDEN: LODs/LOD_B .. LOD_H (the lower levels of detail of the game, each a complete car with its wheels in place; 21 exports hold LOD_A only), Variants/<kind> (damaged panels, broken lights and glass, lit lamps and glows, motion-blur wheels, bonnet-camera copies of body and bonnet, pop-up lamps up) and Cockpit/LOD_* (the in-car model with dashboard and driver's arms).  LODs/no_name: groups whose names the export lost.","Variants/at_origin: parts that the game hangs on hinge points which the export does not have, so they sit at the origin (under the floor): the steering wheels, the fans of the 909 and 917K, the moving rear wings of the SLR 722, Reventon, One-77 and CX75, and 2 cm stand-ins for doors / mirrors of race cars that have none.  The steering wheel is therefore missing inside the visible car.","WHEELS: the game models ONE wheel (rim, tyre, disc, calipers; some cars a rear wheel of their own) and puts it on the car's wheel points; here it is copied onto the 4 points (the right side mirrored).  The points come from the lowest LOD, where the game has the 4 wheels in place (LOD_F_WHEEL; checked against the game's own points file of the Civic: within 1 mm): 91 cars, the 1951 F375 from its nameless groups (its export lost the names and materials of the wheels: tyre plain rubber, the rest with the wheel picture).  The exports with LOD_A only have no such LOD: for 19 of them the points are measured from the wheel arches of the body (tested on the cars that do have LOD_F: axle within 1.5 cm, height within 2 cm for 80 % of the wheels): 1967_shelby_cobra_gt500, 1998_mercedes_clk_lm, 2002_mazda_rx7_spiritr, 2004_ferrari_f430, 2008_mazda_furai, 2008_spada_codatronca_ts, 2010_bmw_m3gts, 2010_ferrari_599_gto, 2010_lamborghini_sesto_elemento, 2011_nissan_gtr, 2011_pagani_huayra, 2011_spada_codatronca_barchetta, 2012_astonmartin_one77, 2012_bmw_1m, 2012_bmw_m6coupe, 2012_ferrari_ff, 2012_lamborghini_aventador, 2013_astonmartin_gt3, 2013_jaguar_cx75; for the open-wheel 2011_lotus_t125 and 2013_ktm_x_bow_r from the ends of the suspension arms (an estimate)."],"tags":["real-racing-3"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["1951_ferrari_f1_f375","",6553536,"real-racing-3","car-1951_ferrari_f1_f375.zip","thumbs/real-racing-3/cars/car-1951_ferrari_f1_f375.webp"],["1957_ferrari_500_trc","",11270154,"real-racing-3","car-1957_ferrari_500_trc.zip","thumbs/real-racing-3/cars/car-1957_ferrari_500_trc.webp"],["1959_porsche_718","",9124154,"real-racing-3","car-1959_porsche_718.zip","thumbs/real-racing-3/cars/car-1959_porsche_718.webp"],["1962_chevrolet_corvette_grand_sport","",11543997,"real-racing-3","car-1962_chevrolet_corvette_grand_sport.zip","thumbs/real-racing-3/cars/car-1962_chevrolet_corvette_grand_sport.webp"],["1967_chevrolet_camaro_ss","",7910039,"real-racing-3","car-1967_chevrolet_camaro_ss.zip","thumbs/real-racing-3/cars/car-1967_chevrolet_camaro_ss.webp"],["1967_shelby_cobra_gt500","",5129452,"real-racing-3","car-1967_shelby_cobra_gt500.zip","thumbs/real-racing-3/cars/car-1967_shelby_cobra_gt500.webp"],["1968_chevrolet_camaro_z28","",10309830,"real-racing-3","car-1968_ch